%% alt: Entity diagram of the Power BI model. One Menu row relates to many Orders rows through the item column: each item appears in many order lines. A Calendar table could relate to Orders through order_date; it is added later in the course. Orders is the fact table, Menu and Calendar are dimension tables, which together form a star.
erDiagram
  MENU ||--o{ ORDERS : "item (one to many)"
  CALENDAR ||..o{ ORDERS : "order_date (added later)"
  MENU {
    string item PK
    string category
    float list_price
  }
  ORDERS {
    int order_id
    datetime order_time
    string item FK
    int qty
    float unit_price
    string payment
    string customer_type
    float line_total
  }
  CALENDAR {
    date date PK
    int month
    string weekday
  }
